<!--p:--><tr bgcolor="#f7f7f7"><td valign=top width=200><a name="POST11966"><font face="Verdana" size="1"><b><!--email--><a href="mailto:vscantu1@msn.com" target="_blank"><!--/email--><!--name-->Vscantu<!--/name--></b></a>
</a><br>Username: <!--field:uname-->Vscantu<!--/field--><br><br>Registered: <!--field:registered-->12-2004<!--/field--><br><!--field:ip_address--><!--/field--></font></font></td><td valign=top><font face="Verdana" size="1"><table width=100% border=0 cellspacing=0 cellpadding=0><tr><td align=left><font face="Verdana" size="1">Posted on Monday, March 21, 2005 - 5:51 pm: &nbsp;&nbsp;</font></td><td align=right></td></tr></table><hr noshade size=0><!--Text-->This is for Questions we may have of Law Enforcement and their Answers to members of this CATCHBTK board. <BR> <BR>Could be for the D.A., police, sherriffs, F.B.I., etc. <BR> <BR>Don&#39;t know if we&#39;ll get any takers, but it sure would be nice &amp; may even help prosecution of the case. It should definitely help bring peace of mind to those involved or interested in the BTK case. <BR> <BR>Please be respectful of each other. <BR> <BR>Victor<!--/Text--></td></tr>
<!--/Post: 11966-->
<!--Post: 12070--><!--Time: 1111549053-->
<!--p:--><tr bgcolor="#cccccc"><td valign=top width=200><a name="POST12070"><font face="Verdana" size="1"><b><!--email--><!--/email--><!--name-->Pax56<!--/name--></b></a><br>Username: <!--field:uname-->Pax56<!--/field--><br><br>Registered: <!--field:registered-->12-2004<!--/field--><br><!--field:ip_address--><!--/field--></font></font></td><td valign=top><font face="Verdana" size="1"><table width=100% border=0 cellspacing=0 cellpadding=0><tr><td align=left><font face="Verdana" size="1">Posted on Tuesday, March 22, 2005 - 7:37 pm: &nbsp;&nbsp;</font></td><td align=right></td></tr></table><hr noshade size=0><!--Text-->It&#39;s a great idea.  I&#39;ll go first if others are shy. <BR> <BR>First off, congratulations and thanks to LE.  You guys put a classic finish on this chess game.  I will never look at a floppy disk without thinking of Rader&#39;s apprehension.  Also, thanks for treating the web sleuths as respectfully as you did.  When I heard that you gave one of our bunch an hour of your time to hear their theory, I was quite frankly awed by your professionalism. <BR> <BR>I&#39;ll try to keep this question at a high level so you can &#40;hopefully&#41; answer it.  It has to do with the role of circumstantial evidence.  Do you see a need for circumstantial evidence in this case?  We are all aware of the preponderance of DNA evidence in this case, making it seem somewhat unnecessary to go into great detail in placing Rader at the scene of the crimes.  Nevertheless, I think the public is rightfully curious about this, as I imagine a jury would also be.  Any comments that any members of LE &#40;our own members or otherwise&#41; would have on the role of circumstantial evidence in this case - without compromising the case itself - would be of interest.  Thanks!  -pax<!--/Text--></td></tr>
<!--/Post: 12070-->
<!--Post: 12134--><!--Time: 1111626665-->
